  "select-a-fragment-with-the-mouse-or-a-finger-a-color-palette-pop": "Select a fragment with the mouse or a finger \u2014 a color palette pops up. Click an existing highlight to change its color or remove it.",
  "create-a-note-from-a-highlight": "Create a note from a highlight",
  "right-click-the-highlighted-text-create-new-note-the-note-is-cre": 'Right-click the highlighted text \u2192 "Create new note". The note is created from your template in the chosen folder, with the quote and a link to the book.',
  "export-all-highlights": "Export all highlights",
  "the-button-at-the-top-of-the-highlights-panel-collects-all-of-th": `The button at the top of the "Highlights" panel. Collects all of the book's highlights at once. It asks for a format: one shared note with all quotes, a separate file per highlight, or inserting all quotes as text straight into the linked book note.`,
  "where-the-from-link-in-highlight-notes-points-empty-the-book-s-f": `Where the "\u2014 from [[\u2026]]" link in highlight notes points. Empty \u2014 the book's file name.`,
  "open-a-book-first": "Open a book first\u2026",
  "choose-from-the-list": "Choose from the list\u2026",
  "no-notes-in-the-vault": "No notes in the vault",
  "a-template-just-for-this-book-for-example-per-genre-empty-the-sh": "A template just for this book (for example, per genre). Empty \u2014 the shared template from the plugin settings is used.",
  "templates-template-md": "Templates/Template.md",
  "about-autosave": "About autosave",
  "your-position-is-saved-automatically-on-every-page-turn-and-kept": `Your position is saved automatically on every page turn and kept in a shared file that syncs across devices (Obsidian Sync). Rebuilding the page (resizing the window, panels, zoom) no longer moves or re-saves progress \u2014 so it won't "drift" on its own.`,
  "welcome-to-book-reader": "Welcome to Book Reader!",
  "it-s-a-cozy-book-reader-right-inside-obsidian-read-highlight-wha": "It's a cozy book reader right inside Obsidian. Read, highlight what matters and turn highlights into notes \u2014 without leaving your vault.",
  "flip-through-a-few-screens-with-the-arrow-or-the-next-button-it": 'Flip through a few screens with the \u2192 arrow (or the "Next" button). It takes a minute, but then everything will be clear.',
  "which-formats-and-how-to-open-a-book": "Which formats, and how to open a book",
  "the-reader-opens-two-formats-epub-epub-files-and-pdf-pdf-files": "The reader supports many formats: Markdown, TXT, HTML, EPUB, PDF, FB2, MOBI, AZW3 and CBZ.",
  "to-read-a-book-put-its-file-into-your-obsidian-vault-and-just-cl": "To read a book, put its file into your Obsidian vault and just click it \u2014 it opens in the reader.",
  "in-the-left-sidebar-there-s-a-library-icon-all-your-books-with-c": `In the left sidebar there's a \u{1F4D6} "Library" icon \u2014 all your books with covers in one place.`,
  "this-is-the-very-first-version": "This is the very first version",
  "please-don-t-load-a-lot-of-books-at-once-start-with-two-or-three": "Please don't load a lot of books at once. Start with two or three and check that everything works reliably on your device.",
  "be-especially-careful-with-very-large-pdfs-hundreds-of-pages-or": "Be especially careful with very large PDFs (hundreds of pages or scanned images) \u2014 they're heavy and may lag.",
  "the-plugin-will-keep-getting-better-for-now-little-by-little-and": "The plugin will keep getting better. For now \u2014 little by little and gently \u{1F642}",
  "highlights-colors-and-actions": "Highlights: colors and actions",
  "select-text-with-a-finger-or-the-mouse-a-palette-appears-pick-a": "Select text with a finger or the mouse \u2014 a palette appears. Pick a color and the highlight is saved.",
  "tap-an-existing-highlight-the-same-menu-opens-change-color-copy": 'Tap an existing highlight \u2014 the same menu opens: change color, copy, set a "stopped here" bookmark, create a note, send it to the book note, or delete.',
  "all-of-the-book-s-highlights-are-gathered-in-the-panel-at-the-to": "All of the book's highlights are gathered in the \u{1F58D}\uFE0F panel at the top \u2014 from there you can jump to any of them or export them all at once.",
  "what-a-book-note-is": 'What a "book note" is',
  "for-each-book-you-can-keep-one-ordinary-obsidian-note-its-home-p": 'For each book you can keep one ordinary Obsidian note \u2014 its "home page", for example "The Master and Margarita.md".',
  "when-you-create-a-note-from-a-highlight-it-links-back-to-this-bo": "When you create a note from a highlight, it links back to this book note. You can also send quotes straight into it \u2014 so all your thoughts on the book gather in one place.",
  "you-don-t-have-to-set-this-up-right-now-you-can-link-a-book-note": `You don't have to set this up right now \u2014 you can link a book note at any time later. Open the book, press the \u24D8 (help) icon at the top of the reader and fill in the "Book note for links" field. Until something is linked, links simply point to the book's file name.`,
  "where-everything-is-stored": "Where everything is stored",
  "your-reading-progress-and-highlights-are-stored-as-files-right-i": `Your reading progress and highlights are stored as files right in the vault (next to the books or in a separate folder \u2014 it's configurable). Nothing is hidden "inside the plugin" \u2014 it's all yours.`,
  "highlight-notes-and-book-notes-are-ordinary-md-notes-in-your-fol": "Highlight notes and book notes are ordinary .md notes in your folder. Open, edit and link them like any others.",
  "about-syncing": "About syncing",
  "since-progress-and-highlights-are-files-in-the-vault-they-sync-a": "Since progress and highlights are files in the vault, they sync along with it (Obsidian Sync, iCloud, etc.).",
  "let-syncing-finish-before-opening-the-same-book-on-another-devic": `Let syncing finish before opening the same book on another device, and don't read one book on two devices at once \u2014 otherwise the position may "argue with itself".`,
  "the-path-to-the-books-folder-can-differ-across-devices-check-the": "The path to the books folder can differ across devices \u2014 check the folders in the plugin settings.",
  "example-how-it-all-works": "Example: how it all works",
